h corpus. When the items are words, n-grams may also be called shingles.[1]  An n-gram of size 1 is referred to as a \"unigram\"; size 2 is a \"bigram\" (or, less commonly, a \"digram\"); size 3 is a \"trigram\". Larger sizes are sometimes referred to by the value of n, e.g., \"four-gram\", \"five-gram\", and so on.","topics":[],"score":213822,"global_rank":252659},{"name":"acheamponge/Bored_Python","owner":"acheamponge","html_url":"https://github.com/acheamponge/Bored_Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"Just me having fun just cos","topics":[],"score":213819,"global_rank":252669},{"name":"rachfop/rock-paper-scissors","owner":"rachfop","html_url":"https://github.com/rachfop/rock-paper-scissors","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":213817,"global_rank":252672},{"name":"lantzbuilds/sqlalchemy-update-minilecture","owner":"lantzbuilds","html_url":"https://github.com/lantzbuilds/sqlalchemy-update-minilecture","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":213817,"global_rank":252678},{"name":"Rasenku/cs1.2-into-data-structures","owner":"Rasenku","html_url":"https://github.com/Rasenku/cs1.2-into-data-structures","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":1,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":213816,"global_rank":252687},{"name":"davidzhangxm/3DMIP-MRIQC","owner":"davidzhangxm","html_url":"https://github.com/davidzhangxm/3DMIP-MRIQC","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":213816,"global_rank":252688},{"name":"nielshanson/dylan-project","owner":"nielshanson","html_url":"https://github.com/nielshanson/dylan-project","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":213813,"global_rank":252707},{"name":"aryann/docdrop","owner":"aryann","html_url":"https://github.com/ary